@startuml

title Timeout: every wait has a limit, and silence becomes a failure

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

participant "caller" as c
participant "callee\n(slow or gone)" as s

c -> s : request (timeout T)
... T passes with no reply ...
c -> c : fail the call: timeout, naming the subject
c -> c : log the correlation id of the request it gave up on
note over c, s
  The callee may still finish. The caller must not assume
  the work was not done, so the work must be safe to repeat.
  A step states its own deadline; the engine fails a silent step
  and stops the run rather than compensating it.
end note
@enduml
